From: Eric Berquist <eric.berquist@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] python3Packages.rdkit: install .dist-info metadata

rdkit is built by CMake with `pyproject = false`, so what lands in
site-packages is a bare rdkit/ tree with no .dist-info beside it. The
package imports perfectly; it is simply invisible to importlib.metadata.

That is what pythonRuntimeDepsCheckHook uses to resolve a wheel's
Requires-Dist, so every dependant that declares rdkit in its own metadata
fails its build:

    Checking runtime dependencies for qmzyme-0.1.2-py3-none-any.whl
      - rdkit not installed

while rdkit is in the closure and importable. The workaround at each
dependant is `pythonRemoveDeps = [ "rdkit" ]`, which drops a declaration
that is true rather than fixing the package it points at.

METADATA alone is enough and is all this writes: importlib.metadata needs
a <name>-<version>.dist-info directory with a Name and a Version, and
reads nothing else. A RECORD would have to carry real hashes to be worth
anything, and nothing consumes one here.

---
--- a/pkgs/development/python-modules/rdkit/default.nix
+++ b/pkgs/development/python-modules/rdkit/default.nix
@@ -184,6 +184,19 @@
     (lib.cmakeFeature "coordgen_DIR" "${coordgenlibs}/lib/cmake")
   ];
 
+  # The CMake build installs the rdkit/ tree straight into site-packages with
+  # no .dist-info beside it, so the package is invisible to
+  # importlib.metadata. Every dependant that declares rdkit in its own
+  # metadata then fails pythonRuntimeDepsCheckHook with "rdkit not installed"
+  # while rdkit sits in its closure, importable. Synthesise the minimum that
+  # importlib.metadata reads: a Name and a Version.
+  postInstall = ''
+    distInfo="$out/${python.sitePackages}/rdkit-${version}.dist-info"
+    mkdir -p "$distInfo"
+    printf 'Metadata-Version: 2.1\nName: rdkit\nVersion: %s\n' \
+      "${version}" >"$distInfo/METADATA"
+  '';
+
   checkPhase = ''
     export QT_QPA_PLATFORM='offscreen'
     export RDBASE=$(realpath ..)
